</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/2895</identifier><datestamp>2026-05-26T19:02:46Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_5</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_276</setSpec></header><metadata><mets xmlns="http://www.loc.gov/METS/" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" ID="&#xa;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;DSpace_ITEM_1843-2895" TYPE="DSpace ITEM" PROFILE="DSpace METS SIP Profile 1.0" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.loc.gov/METS/ http://www.loc.gov/standards/mets/mets.xsd" OBJID="&#xa;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;&#x9;hdl:1843/2895">
   <metsHdr CREATEDATE="2026-11-10T09:23:22Z">
      <agent ROLE="CUSTODIAN" TYPE="ORGANIZATION">
         <name>"Repositório Institucional da UFMG"</name>
      </agent>
   </metsHdr>
   <dmdSec ID="DMD_1843_2895">
      <mdWrap MDTYPE="MODS">
         <xmlData xmlns:mods="http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3 http://www.loc.gov/standards/mods/v3/mods-3-1.xsd">
            <mods:mods xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3 http://www.loc.gov/standards/mods/v3/mods-3-1.xsd">
               <mods:extension>
                  <mods:dateAccessioned encoding="iso8601">2026-05-26T19:02:46Z</mods:dateAccessioned>
               </mods:extension>
               <mods:originInfo>
                  <mods:dateIssued encoding="iso8601">2024-11-11</mods:dateIssued>
               </mods:originInfo>
               <mods:identifier type="uri">https://hdl.handle.net/1843/2895</mods:identifier>
               <mods:abstract>Diabetes Mellitus is a comorbidity characterized by multiple signs and symptoms resulting from
alterations in the metabolism of fats, carbohydrates, and proteins, leading to elevated blood
glucose levels and reduced cellular ability to utilize glucose effectively. This Intervention
Project (IP) was developed with the purpose of providing a prompt assessment of the local
problem, based on data obtained from electronic medical records, which revealed a high number
of decompensated diabetic patients. In view of this scenario, the need for a nonpharmacological approach was identified, focusing on the analysis of dietary habits among
individuals diagnosed with Diabetes Mellitus within the population assigned to the Family
Health Unit (USF). The objective of this project is to develop and implement a nutritional menu
using foods readily available in the region, aimed at diabetic patients registered at the Dr. João
Costa Family Health Unit, located in Barreiros, Pernambuco, Brazil. The intervention seeks to
promote Diabetes Mellitus control through adequate, accessible, and sustainable dietary
strategies, emphasizing non-drug treatment and improvement in patients’ quality of life. The
implementation steps include: meetings with the health team; active search for patients
diagnosed with Diabetes Mellitus; educational activities held every 15 days; weight
measurement and body mass index (BMI) calculation after each session; and periodic
reassessments to reinforce guidance provided during educational interventions. The
presentation and execution of the nutritional menu will involve the participation of the
multidisciplinary team — including a physician, nurse, nursing technician, community health
agents, and a nutritionist from the e-MULTI program. After project implementation, it is
expected that participants will experience reduced blood glucose levels, improved glycated
hemoglobin rates, and weight loss in follow-up evaluations conducted at three and six months.
Throughout the 12-month execution period, approximately 60% to 65% of the patients are
expected to maintain continuous follow-up and demonstrate measurable progress, benefiting
from dietary and lifestyle changes that contribute not only to diabetes control but also to an
overall improvement in quality of life.</mods:abstract>
               <mods:language>
                  <mods:languageTerm authority="rfc3066" />
               </mods:language>
               <mods:accessCondition type="useAndReproduction">Acesso aberto Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivs 3.0 Brazil</mods:accessCondition>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Nutrição dos Grupos Vulneráveis</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Atenção Primária à Saúde</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Dissertação Acadêmica</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:titleInfo>
                  <mods:title>Projeto de intervenção: criação de cardápio nutricional através de alimentos disponíveis na região para controle do Diabetes Mellitus dos pacientes diabéticos cadastrados na Unidade de Saúde da Família Dr João Costa em Barreiros PE</mods:title>
               </mods:titleInfo>
               <mods:genre>Trabalho de conclusão de curso</mods:genre>
            </mods:mods>
         </xmlData>
      </mdWrap>
   </dmdSec>
